---
/**
 * Privacy Policy page (AC-10)
 * Public page — no auth required.
 */
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout title="Privacy Policy">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl px-4 py-12 space-y-8 text-sm text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
    <div>
      <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="text-gray-500 text-xs">Last updated: {new Date().getFullYear()}</p>
    </div>

    <section class="space-y-2">
      <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-gray-800">1. What we collect</h2>
      <p>
        FitHub collects the following data to provide its service: your email address from OAuth
        sign-in, fitness activity data (duration, distance, type, start time) from connected
        platforms (Zwift, Strava), sync job records, and session cookies for authentication.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-2">
      <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-gray-800">2. How we use your data</h2>
      <p>
        Your fitness data is stored solely to power the FitHub dashboard — allowing you to view
        a unified history across platforms. We do not sell, share, or use your data for advertising.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-2">
      <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-gray-800">3. Cookies</h2>
      <p>
        We use a single, strictly necessary session cookie (<code>fithub_session</code>) to keep
        you authenticated. No tracking or advertising cookies are set.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-2">
      <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-gray-800">4. Data deletion</h2>
      <p>
        You can delete your account and all associated data at any time from the{" "}
        <a href="/settings" class="text-brand-600 hover:underline">Settings</a> page.
        Deletion is immediate and permanent.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-2">
      <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-gray-800">5. Third-party platforms</h2>
      <p>
        When you connect Zwift or Strava, you authorise FitHub to read activity data on your
        behalf via their OAuth APIs. FitHub does not store OAuth access tokens beyond their
        immediate use; refresh tokens are encrypted at rest.
      </p>
    </section>

    <p class="text-gray-400 text-xs">
      Questions? Contact us at <a href="mailto:privacy@fithub.app" class="underline">privacy@fithub.app</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</Layout>
